**PR title and description must not mention the beads tracker.** Beads is a
local, repo-internal task tracker; its IDs are meaningless to a reader of the
pull request. Keep out of both the title and the body:

- bead IDs in any form (`mitto-abc`, `beads:mitto-abc`, `#mitto-abc`)
- `(refs <bead-id>)` footers copied from commit messages
- `bd` commands, and phrases like "beads issue", "the bead", "closes the epic"

Describe the change in reader-facing terms instead — what behavior changed,
why, and how it was verified. Referencing a real upstream issue tracker
(GitHub issues, JIRA) is fine; only the beads tracker is excluded.

Because commits in this repo carry `(refs <bead-id>)` footers, **never pass
the `--fill` flag** to `gh pr create` / `glab mr create` when any commit on
the branch references a bead — that flag copies commit bodies verbatim into
the PR. Write an explicit title and body instead:

```bash
gh pr create --title "<title>" --body "<body>" --base <target-branch>
```

If the body contains backticks or other shell-hostile characters, write it to
a temporary file first and pass `--body-file <path>`.
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
